    "title": "Linda Yasenak",
    "text": "May 18, 1951 - June 21, 2025\nLinda Yasenak, 74, passed away on June 21, 2025, in Clinton, Tennessee after battling cancer.\nBorn on May 18, 1951, in Idaho Falls, Idaho, Linda grew up in Missoula, Montana with her brother and two sisters. She attended Hellgate High School and married Patrick Yasenak. Together they had four children and later divorced. Linda then relocated to Tennessee, where she spent her remaining years.\nLinda was a creative spirit who found joy in crafting, painting, quilting, and decorating her home. Her garage wall was adorned with wreaths she had made over the years. She also enjoyed gardening and loved being with her pets. She loved spending time with family, especially during the holidays.\nShe is survived by her children: Tyler Yasenak (Carol) and his sons Xander and Hunter; Stephanie Winter (Chris) and their children Jake and Marissa; Philip Yasenak and his son Wyatt; and Nicholas Yasenak (Mary) and his daughter Erycka.\nLinda was preceded in death by her granddaughter Kaylee Yasenak.\nIn accordance with her wishes, no fuss was to be made after she passes, so no services are planned and only a very simply obituary was written. Linda was a private person who found fulfillment in the simple joys of life and the company of those closest to her.\nMay her memory bring comfort to those who knew her.",
